  "id": "lok_dayro",
  "name": "Lok dayro (Saurashtra song-and-story session)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Dayro (lok dayro) is an evening gathering of Saurashtra in which folk singers and storytellers sit before an audience and alternate bhajans, folk songs, sung couplets (duha) and humorous or heroic stories, often until dawn; a santvani is a dayro given over to the bhajans of saint-poets. Sung to harmonium, tabla and cymbals, it circulates widely on commercial cassettes and recordings, with performers such as Hemant Chauhan and Praful Dave.",
  "recipe": "classic modern lok dayro, ballad Poetry, indian bard branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. song accompaniment straight harmonium indian, pitched indian rosewood rosewood tabla, manjira. festival stage. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
